  "summary": "I reconciled all five St. Brigid discharges under RBC-TOC-02 and wrote a progress note for each. Results and documents that came in while I worked changed four of my decisions, and I corrected them. Five items need your decision (listed at the end).\n\n**Walter Kim (pt-0005)**\n- **Furosemide:** changed to 40 mg twice daily (mr-t0001). The signed addendum (doc-00009) overrides the summary's 40 mg daily. An unsigned draft addendum that arrived during my work proposed 60 mg twice daily (doc-00902). Only a signed addendum counts, so I ignored it.\n- **Potassium chloride:** stopped, per the discharge summary.\n- **Omeprazole:** kept. Pantoprazole was only the hospital's formulary substitute, so I didn't order it.\n- **Lisinopril (mr-00072):** at first I left it on hold, because his 10/21 potassium was 5.4. A repeat lab drawn 10/23 then came in with potassium 4.7 and creatinine 1.21. That meets the discharge condition (creatinine under 1.5), so I resumed it.\n- **Leftover task:** the review task I made for you earlier (task-t0003) is no longer needed. The system wouldn't let me cancel it, so please close it.\n- Metoprolol XL, atorvastatin and aspirin continue unchanged.\n\n**Terence Stark (pt-0004)**\n- **Carvedilol:** I raised it to 12.5 mg twice daily per the summary. Then a signed addendum arrived (doc-00904): his heart rate was 48–52 with lightheadedness, and the increase was reversed before discharge. I changed it back to 6.25 mg twice daily (mr-t0016), so his dose is the same as before admission.\n- Aspirin and insulin 70/30 continue.\n\n**Earnest Roberts (pt-0044)**\n- **Lisinopril (mr-00373):** at first I resumed it on the 10/22 labs (creatinine 1.08, potassium 4.6). A new potassium of 5.5 on 10/23 arrived, so I put it back on hold. Task for you due 10/27 (task-t0019).\n- Glargine, lispro and rosuvastatin continue.\n\n**Gerald Whitcomb (pt-0069)**\n- **Lisinopril (mr-69003):** at first I resumed it on the 10/21 labs (creatinine 1.12, potassium 4.4). A potassium of 5.4 drawn 10/22 then came in, so I put it back on hold. Task for you due 10/26 (task-t0020).\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin continue.\n\n**Lorraine Pruitt (pt-0067)**\n- **Metformin (mr-67001):** stays on hold. Her only creatinine (1.21) was drawn in the hospital before discharge, and the instruction requires a post-discharge result. Task for you due 10/24, when her post-discharge lab is expected (task-t0013).\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin continue.\n\n**Flagged for you:**\n1. **Stark, atorvastatin:** his last fill was 3/4/26, covering only about 24% of the 180 days before admission. I left the order unchanged and messaged you (comm-t0006).\n2. **Stark, glipizide:** an outside endocrinologist, Dr. Desai, prescribes it and the discharge summary doesn't mention it. I didn't order or change anything and messaged you (comm-t0007).\n3. **Roberts and Whitcomb, lisinopril:** both are on hold because of high potassium; see the tasks above.\n4. **Pruitt, metformin:** waiting on her post-discharge lab; see the task above.\n\nAll five new results/documents that arrived in the inbox while I worked are closed out.",
